    "belowThreshold": "may know holidays and polite respect; no deep practice or denomination identity",
    "atOrAbove50": "attach 1 denomination/path (weighted 95% christian_main) + 1-2 practice/attitude subs; can name church style in talk",
    "atOrAbove70": "faith shapes week and conflict; history hooks (conversion, church hurt, family pressure) unlock under trust",
    "extreme95": "faith is primary identity lens; most decisions filtered through it; rivalBias can heat denomination arguments",
    "oddRoll": "5% other/none cluster keeps the town from feeling cloned—Muslim, Jewish, atheist, pagan, etc. stay rare but real"
  },
  "notes": "Do not preach at the player from every NPC. Private faith is common. rivalBias true for denomination and politics-from-pulpit friction. Amish/Mennonite pockets matter for Ohio flavor but stay uncommon in the 200 actives unless location calls for it."
